 the year, ending as Mojo Dojo Casa Team."},{"season":"2024","heading":"2024: Mojo Dojo Casa Team","text":"Under Emily and Riley, Mojo Dojo Casa Team went 8-6 to finish as the No. 5 seed, scoring 1997.78 points, 2nd in the league. Their all-play record of 111-43 suggests a team that was better than its record; schedule luck was worth 2.09 wins against them. [[p:4984|Josh Allen]] led the club with 379.04 points in 16 starts, followed by [[p:4866|Saquon Barkley]] (355.30). The season high was 224.94 in week 15 ([[g:2024-15-1-2]]). In the Dynasty Playoffs they beat [[f:2|Storm FC]] 224.94-144.90 in the First Round, then beat [[f:8|Breece is the Word]] 147.72-147.12 in the Semifinal, then beat [[f:5|i’m Stroud of you]] 163.78-100.56 in the Dynasty Championship and won the championship ring. The front office made 39 transactions, 10 of them trades."},{"season":"2025","heading":"2025: Mojo Dojo Casa Team","text":"Under Emily and Riley, Mojo Dojo Casa Team went 10-4 to finish as the No. 4 seed, scoring 1950.26 points, 4th in the league. [[p:4984|Josh Allen]] led the club with 364.62 points in 16 starts, followed by [[p:8130|Trey McBride]] (302.40). The season high was 190.18 in week 15 ([[g:2025-15-1-9]]). In the Dynasty Playoffs they beat [[f:9|Clandestine Ball Busters]] 190.18-151.56 in the First Round, then lost to [[f:8|BBL KIZZY]] 137.14-146.62 in the Semifinal, then beat [[f:5|St. Brown VS Board]] 135.14-125.88 in the Third Place Game and finished 3rd. The front office made 47 transactions, 10 of them trades."},{"season":"2026","heading":"2026: Mojo Dojo Casa Team 💍","text":"Through 4 games under Emily and Riley, Mojo Dojo Casa Team 💍 are 4-0 and 1st in the standings, with 682.08 points (2nd). [[p:4984|Josh Allen]] led the club with 115.76 points in 4 starts, followed by [[p:8150|Kyren Williams]] (96.60). The season high was 183.58 in week 4 ([[g:2026-04-1-10]]). The front office made 23 transactions, 3 of them trades. The club was renamed 2 times during the year, ending as Mojo Dojo Casa Team 💍."}]}